# Project One Get-Item Pseudocode
#
# Graded checkpoint: Module Five Project One
# Later use: get-item and inventory design for M7 Project Two
#
# Review the course-provided get-item flowchart before completing this file.
# Write pseudocode, not Python code. Use clear indentation and course-appropriate
# keywords such as INPUT, OUTPUT, IF, ELSE, SET, ADD, or similar terms.

IF the player enters "get item":

    Check the current room.

    IF the current room contains an item:

        Display:
            "There is an item in this room."

        Ask:
            "What item would you like to get?"

        Get the player's input.

        Convert the input to lowercase.

        IF the item entered matches the item in the current room:

            Add the item to the player's inventory.

            Remove the item from the room.

            Display:
                "You collected the [item]."

            Display the player's inventory.

        ELSE:

            Display:
                "That item is not in this room."
            Display:
                "Please enter the correct item."

    ELSE:

        Display:
            "There is no item in this room."

    IF the player's inventory contains all six items:

        Display:
            "You have collected all six items!"
            "You can now escape the underwater station."

END IF


